{"step_index":63,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T20:13:54Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T01:43:54+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T01:44:00+05:30\nThe search for \"Unsloth fine-tune Qwen 2.5 3B complete tutorial code 2025 2026 step by step\" returned the following summary:\nTo fine-tune a **Qwen 2.5 3B** model using Unsloth, you can leverage the library's highly optimized kernels which provide 2x faster training and 60-70% less VRAM usage compared to standard methods[1][2][3].\n\nBelow is the step-by-step approach and code structure to perform this fine-tuning[4].\n\n### 1. Prerequisites and Environment Setup\nYou can run this on a free **Google Colab Tesla T4 GPU**[1][5]. Install the necessary dependencies first:\n\n```bash\npip install unsloth\npip install \"unsloth[colab-new] @ git+https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth.git\"\npip install --no-deps xformers trl peft accelerate bitsandbytes\n```\n\n### 2. Implementation Code\nThis script demonstrates how to load the model, apply LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation), and prepare for training[4].\n\n```python\nfrom unsloth import FastLanguageModel\nfrom datasets import load_dataset\nfrom trl import SFTTrainer\nfrom transformers import TrainingArguments\n\n# 1. Load Model and Tokenizer\nmodel, tokenizer = FastLanguageModel.from_pretrained(\n    model_name=\"Qwen/Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct\",\n    max_seq_length=2048,\n    load_in_4bit=True, # Enables efficient memory usage\n)\n\n# 2. Add LoRA Adapters\nmodel = FastLanguageModel.get_peft_model(\n    model,\n    r=16, # Rank: higher = more parameters to train\n    lora_alpha=32,\n    lora_dropout=0.1,\n    target_modules=[\"q_proj\", \"k_proj\", \"v_proj\", \"o_proj\", \n                    \"gate_proj\", \"up_proj\", \"down_proj\"],\n)\n\n# 3. Load and Format Dataset\n# Ensure your dataset is in a chat format (e.g., {\"messages\": [...]})\ndataset = load_dataset(\"your-dataset-name\", split=\"train\")\n\n# 4. Initialize Trainer\ntrainer = SFTTrainer(\n    model=model,\n    train_dataset=dataset,\n    dataset_text_field=\"text\", # Or use data_collator for chat formats\n    max_seq_length=2048,\n    args=TrainingArguments(\n        per_device_train_batch_size=2,\n        gradient_\n<truncated 1687 bytes>\nVIVPw2Q2o2F6rhZyX6PdaxRyM4qTxRq08PlAKQX8Z-1zRyBSGqajZCCUwYhUqMYuScqu70ijrExtm3uQvbB0WOiWh3idmR)\n[3] [huggingface.co](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG_mJ2rSkIy8SONxIywEZWnhyYAiSpO_JMd2bgwArtKadFbd8uHgmvvwc9PwhCRwt4PyYSNkrzF3qeP0vpQ0tDOk7KpipraVavlro8EZIjYLtGEu9Xt1qU9EWng5LZHSJ-xAGYxGXxLPw==)\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHT4DJWgrcIMOcVd8QtNhcTeFpUEm5qi6a4QjoQsB7lJ6IMcaGXKZYpi7u2dW58V7xqVYSmezkK77NjqWHsXDEaKcPc14SqD3WY5t2pKmd4NznEB2wNdaHbeCNevQ9o1maIn47v6A==)\n[5] [towardsai.net](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGehBRCAhytxjOMiykKRL3sP80WSNg6ZiB-l_3XQZlv2t4-k64SZiBDOEccE4O2fHHjwJSTnzpmDl73G3Ecas8PJpk8OJEakHD4fv2xrRHnFoKOe1kqfNKaVhEYKNfMXJxi6QcAPFi_D6YJ804EDAlSOkH19yRoq26jfreGQ4U0POvgdGMVPLKGym2r)\n[6] [unsloth.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF26cOA-Lsc-YcdfJad09USoHVIVPw2Q2o2F6rhZyX6PdaxRyM4qTxRq08PlAKQX8Z-1zRyBSGqajZCCUwYhUqMYuScqu70ijrExtm3uQvbB0WOiWh3idmR)\n[7] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHoISnbsKR5zcrVikLnKpUroKhOXPSYeCnWjh2ajmFIqNLT-RCgumJLvEMM3vn6GlpvB1R4m8XXSFUanLCEVnCE8sTYKJgshT3J_usg3cK7qqdteVUxugQorqtcyXsBzTEI)\n[8] [unsloth.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFdDkM9BcmH7tcJaG5kJ7Qrft1Hy6gzjfhI19ztQQvAsp5okuUd7eL0p20CzwAm_MLzS6zjdCoOJfEZIYr89zu-Saqnry36O6ikQvEAUT3RFD4XOYPpeED2VMAuQKxzAA9VFZI1ExTCp25Msg==)\n[9] [kaggle.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGAMRBxR7o8cJa3FmnYG2rRKsK3W63vtkU_ohQkRrNl6EaiFMX-njMFa1i0OHH8G-Bvg3CxmHCdy_9eiBq4Q6inL5YYsfghLc1XUxbCbxG3kRW1s9BRS6f9bcs5wgM07xbmez-kVF3n9v9qgA1